{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedding"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_one_physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_one_physical","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QuantumTrace.lean#L192-L198","doc":"At the physical weight `w = (1, q²)` — the `K = diag(1, q²)` of the corpus's\nSchur–Weyl normalisation — the weighted trace of the identity is `(1 + q²)^{m+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_sigma_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_sigma_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QuantumTrace.lean#L165-L188","doc":"**Cyclicity against a generator.** `tr_w(σ_a · y) = tr_w(y · σ_a)`.\n\nThis is what `braidAt_comm_siteWeight` gives directly: the weight can be moved past the\ngenerator's image, and the ordinary trace is cyclic. Extending it to arbitrary `x` in place\nof `σ_a` would need the whole image to centralise `W`, which is an induction over the\nalgebra rather than over its generators — see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_one","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QuantumTrace.lean#L151-L163","doc":"**The weighted trace of the identity** is the `n`-th power of the total weight,\n`(∑ₖ w k)^{m+1}`.\n\nThis is exactly `QOU.MassTheory.WeightedPermutationCharacter`'s value at the identity\npermutation, so the braiding's weighted trace and the permutation character agree where they\noverlap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QuantumTrace.lean#L145-L149","doc":"**The site-weighted (quantum) trace** of an element of `H_{m+1}(q)`, through the\nR-matrix representation: `tr_w(x) = tr(W · ρ(x))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.braidAt_comm_siteWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.braidAt_comm_siteWeight","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QuantumTrace.lean#L127-L139","doc":"**The braiding commutes with the site weight — for every weight.**\n\nNo hypothesis on `w`. `Ř`'s off-diagonal entries connect `e_i ⊗ e_j` to `e_j ⊗ e_i`, which\ncarry the same site weight, so the weight cannot separate them. This is the Cartan-level\nequivariance of Jimbo's `Ř`, and it is what makes the weighted trace below a *trace*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.prod_weight_eq_of_braidAt_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.prod_weight_eq_of_braidAt_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QuantumTrace.lean#L92-L125","doc":"**A nonzero braiding entry connects states of equal weight.**\n\nThe two cases are the whole reason the commutation below needs no hypothesis on `w`: a\nnonzero entry either sits on the diagonal (`a = b`), or is the swap entry, in which case\n`b = a ∘ (i j)` — and permuting sites leaves `∏ₘ w (a m)` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.prod_weight_comp_equiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.prod_weight_comp_equiv","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QuantumTrace.lean#L79-L82","doc":"Permuting the sites does not change the total weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.siteWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.siteWeight","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QuantumTrace.lean#L73-L77","doc":"The **site-wise weight** on `V^{⊗n}`: the diagonal matrix whose entry at a basis state\n`a` is the product of the per-site weights `∏ₘ w (a m)`. For `w = (1, q²)` this is the\n`K^{⊗n}` of the quantum trace. ","signatureChunk":0}]}